WEBVTT

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.280
Back then, I...

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.050
Can you climb trees?

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.290
I can, but not with these shoes on.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.480
Could you if you took them off?

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.290
What?

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.210
I-I can, but not today.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.800
My socks will get dirty.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.470
Hey, there's a pond over there.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:33.550
Let's go see the fish.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.890
Climb it next time.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.830
<i>Why did I want him</i>

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.280
<i>to climb that tree?</i>

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:53.980
Moyashimon

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.980
Returns

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.900
I'm going to make dinner tonight.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.370
What would you all like?

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.160
Japanese food, I guess.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.630
I like bouillabaisse.

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:30.240
Curry.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.880
Quiet, fools!

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:34.900
It has to be native Burgundy cuisine!

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.510
If you want bouillabaisse, go south!

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:41.510
Why did you ask us, then?

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.510
Local production for local consumption!

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.470
Just because the chef isn't here,

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:48.520
I can't send you home without 
feeding you a local specialty.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:51.420
You did have sashimi with 
soy sauce yesterday.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.920
Bringing soy sauce was 
worth it, huh, Tadayasu?

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.530
Yeah. We didn't eat any, though.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.780
So, Hasegawa-san,

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.720
can we open that Cros 
Parantoux tonight?

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.710
Huh? Oh, of course.

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:06.260
Merci.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.620
I'm really sorry for yester—

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.720
That said, dinner will 
be ready in four hours.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.450
Please take time to chat until then.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:15.040
That's too long...

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:19.920
I'm looking forward to dinner.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:23.140
What will you do until 
dinner, Hasegawa-san?

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.520
We are in a domaine. We could go see—

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:27.080
I'll pass.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.680
Is this what they call a...

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:35.300
"Don't act like my boyfriend just 
because it worked once" thing?

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.380
Oh!

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:40.540
"Oh," what? Nothing happened, idiot.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:44.230
Hey, just a second...

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:45.660
Sawaki.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:50.580
What's going on with Hasegawa-san?

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:52.620
What do you mean?

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:55.060
Didn't you guys come to get her?

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.340
Yeah, but...

00:03:56.850 --> 00:04:00.330
You were worried about Marie, 
too, weren't you, Tadayasu?

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:03.010
Hasegawa-san doesn't want 
to get married, right?

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:07.840
They even sent people here 
from Paris to take her back.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:11.020
I don't really know all 
the details either...

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:13.260
But I think Hasegawa-san is

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.020
staying here because she 
has something in mind.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:20.110
She's always had trouble 
communicating with her father.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:21.540
That's why it turned 
out so complicated.

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:25.060
Sounds like someone else's family...

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.280
What does that mean?

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:28.710
You're interrupting 
my cooking! Go away!

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:33.540
What's her problem?

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:43.510
What should I do?

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:51.680
They're all trying to 
make a fool of me!

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:58.080
For whose sake do they 
think I've been...

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.690
planning all this for months?!

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:14.010
Well? Good, isn't it?

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:15.250
Très bien, right?

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:19.400
It better be good. 
It took four hours to make.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:20.980
Oh, shut up!

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:23.590
It was ready exactly when I said 
it would be! Don't complain!

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:27.970
But this Cros Parantoux 
really is incredible.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:29.740
The moment we opened it,

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:32.970
the whole room smelled 
like a flower garden.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:38.010
Is it really okay to drink it 
with my wine-braised beef?

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:40.600
Well, it really is good.

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:49.240
Your wine braising is exquisite, Marie.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:51.840
I guess it's possible because you know

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.370
the characteristics of the wine.

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:58.000
Would you care for some 
Cros Parantoux, too, sir?

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:00.290
Thank you, young lady.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.550
But I'm still inexperienced,

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.260
so in order to learn more, 
I only drink my own wine.

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:09.040
You can't drink alcohol, either, right?

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:12.180
Want to get some of what 
he's drinking with me?

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:12.640
What?

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.270
There are no wine microbes 
around his drink.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:20.650
I think it's just grape juice.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:21.520
Microbes?

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:24.930
I didn't quite understand all 
of your Japanese there...

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:27.730
But my father always 
prepares his own wine,

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:30.280
separate from what the 
rest of us drink.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.130
You mean...

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.530
Knowing Marie's personality,

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:46.860
I thought she'd check her dad's 
bottle right then and there.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:50.220
I guess there's a sort of awkward 
distance between Marie and her dad.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.980
If that was juice...

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:53.440
Yeah.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:55.780
So the guy's been trying 
hard to make wine,

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:57.600
even though he can't drink it.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.480
Maybe I shouldn't have said that...

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:02.950
No use worrying about that.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:04.820
It won't do us any good.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.620
Where did Marie go?

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:09.570
After dinner, she said she 
was going to the cave.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.380
Hasegawa-san went with her.

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:16.700
I think Marie really wants to 
help her dad with the vineyards.

00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:21.270
I haven't done anything to help

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:23.280
with getting Hasegawa-san 
back, either...

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:24.840
Hey, boy!

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:27.950
Did you tell Marie to 
come to the winery?

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:30.740
We're so cold, we can't brew!

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:36.660
I wonder if Marie went 
to check on the winery.

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:40.270
Her father has a hard 
time taking care of us.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:42.270
Are you sure you don't

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:44.590
want to ask your father about the wine?

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:47.540
I sort of had a feeling 
he'd been doing that.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:52.320
He never brought up the subject 
of the flavor of wine himself.

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:54.870
I didn't think it was 
even worth asking him.

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:59.380
So he was always just pretending 
to drink wine in front of me.

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:02.620
There are sake brewers in 
Japan who can't drink, too.

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:04.030
Yeah...

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:05.990
Fermenting is a science,

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:08.850
so you can make anything as 
long as you can quantify it.

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:09.680
But...

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:13.240
Wouldn't a menu written 
by a chef who loves natto

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:15.930
taste better than one written by a chef

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.260
who can't eat natto?

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.770
Not necessarily...

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:21.980
If you want to call it sense...

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:26.010
if my father had it, he wouldn't 
worry as much as he does.

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:31.340
You have high hopes for 
your father, don't you?

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:32.890
But there are times

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:34.610
when it doesn't look that way to me.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:39.620
I think you should talk 
with your father.

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:42.370
Yeah...

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:46.750
It may sound strange coming from me,

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:48.710
but maybe we've both

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:51.630
been too stubborn to face our fathers.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:54.690
No offense... it's just that I 
heard a little of the story.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:57.690
Not only my father.

00:08:57.690 --> 00:09:02.880
I've never once considered 
Ryuuta-kun's feelings.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:07.900
Okay, let's both go for it tonight.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:10.350
May I use your phone?

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:13.230
I'll have a talk with him, too,

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:15.150
without running away.

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:22.660
It's time for Marie to do 
some brewing of her own.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:25.100
And that other lady, too.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:27.580
I guess all we can do is watch.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.670
If only there was something 
we could do to help...

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:35.670
Hey, Sawaki, what are you going to do?

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:41.180
Who washes a car with wine?

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:45.300
All you yeasts from 
Marie's winery, get over here!

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:48.330
This is for your sakes as much as hers!

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:52.730
I'm going back.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:57.400
Why couldn't that fatty 
come get you himself?

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:00.170
What the hell has this whole 
day been for, anyway?

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:02.240
Why do we all have to go?

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:05.750
I'm scared.

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:07.750
I want...

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:11.620
I want you there to make sure 
I don't try to run away.

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:19.180
What's this?

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:20.870
Are they going out somewhere?

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:26.840
Sorry, Marie, but could I borrow 
that book from you again?

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:28.020
Is it in the cave?

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:29.570
Uh, yeah.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:33.660
There are some other new releases 
that I could recommend, too.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:34.870
Want to read them?

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:36.780
Oh... yes, good idea.

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:39.610
I'll go with you.

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.930
Stay here.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.350
Must be rough, 
having to listen in

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:06.120
while your girlfriend talks 
about breaking up.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:08.850
Idiot! I told you, nothing happened!

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:12.790
Ryuuta-kun...

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:15.530
You know, Haruka-san...

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:16.530
Huh?

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:19.270
I've been under a lot of 
pressure since I was young.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:24.860
I thought I was being 
asked to babysit you,

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:26.980
but before I knew it, both our dads

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:28.620
started to say we were betrothed.

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:31.290
Just when I had resolved myself to it,

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.750
you used college as an 
excuse to run away.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:38.940
I wanted to use this trip 
to figure something out.

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:42.630
I told your father I'd 
hold the ceremony

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:45.130
and told you that this 
was a pre-wedding trip,

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:51.020
but do you guys think I'm 
really that clueless?

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.260
And these are about

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:56.200
all kinds of interesting 
new approaches being taken

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:57.420
in the wine industry.

00:11:57.420 --> 00:11:58.530
Thanks.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:01.160
I'll read them later.

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:06.620
I hear Pierre's going to have to 
let half of his vineyards go.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.720
These are tough times.

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:12.370
The first thing you learn 
when you start to drink wine

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:14.110
is that French wine is expensive,

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:16.420
while it's hard to go 
wrong with New World

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:18.210
wines in this era since they're cheaper.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:22.730
Still, I don't think this 
is how it should be.

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:25.140
This isn't like you, Marie.

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:29.470
What new measures could we 
adopt here in Burgundy?

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:31.940
Everything to be tried has been tried.

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:37.680
Wine making in this region has 
already been long perfected.

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:41.350
I'm not telling you to start planting

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:43.920
white grapes among the 
red ones or anything.

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:46.700
But using screw-on caps 
instead of corks,

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.620
or using cartons or plastic 
bottles instead of glass,

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:52.120
would at least count 
as attempts, right?

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:54.030
Ah, Marie,

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:56.860
I never thought I would 
hear such things from you.

00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:59.090
Perhaps I was mistaken to think

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:02.260
that you would understand 
my duty to uphold tradition.

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:06.430
Even the many types and production 
methods of wine glasses

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:09.010
are young in comparison 
to the history of wine.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:11.310
New methods are constantly being

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:13.740
attempted even in Burgundy and Bordeaux.

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:15.520
What is this about?

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:18.140
What are you trying to say, Marie?

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.480
I have a proposal for you.

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:25.150
First, would you drink some of this?

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:28.590
No, I believe you're aware

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:30.640
that I don't want to drink any wine

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:32.320
but my own and your grandfather's.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:36.790
You mean you can't.

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:43.800
You're making a fool of me!

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:46.420
No, I'm not! Ryuuta-kun, even I...

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:49.450
It's perfectly clear to 
me since we came here.

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:52.020
I thought about everything 
that's happened,

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:53.560
and I want to talk to yo—

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:55.430
Quiet!

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.650
Wait, Dad! Listen to me!

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:02.020
I'm well aware that you love 
our vineyards and wine.

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:06.060
And I'm grateful that you've 
avoided interfering for my sake.

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:09.580
But if you know that I 
can't drink alcohol,

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:11.660
then you were just insulting me!

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:14.290
No, I wasn't! Let me finish!

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:17.370
You think everything I do is wrong!

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.750
But I've been learning from 
your grandfather as well,

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:20.930
and I'm studying hard!

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:22.060
I understand that!

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:23.460
No, you don't understand anything!

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:25.330
I'm talking to you because 
I do understand!

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:26.980
Why do you have to be like this?!

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:31.430
Hasegawa-san, is it going well for you?

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:33.800
I want to talk to you.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:37.060
I'll tell you something that's 
always been on my mind.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:39.920
It's not that I can't climb trees!

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:41.560
I just refuse to!

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:44.050
No, soy un Mexicano.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:47.380
So it's true!

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:49.780
You really are the Mexican 
we saw at the station!

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:51.930
Someone, come quick!

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:55.120
Miss!

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:01.680
H-He just suddenly collapsed...

00:15:02.930 --> 00:15:03.790
Ryuuta-kun!

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.630
Stay back, Hasegawa-san!

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:07.950
I've seen this before!

00:15:08.350 --> 00:15:09.880
It's norovirus!

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:18.390
What is this?

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:21.310
"We're cold, Marie."

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:24.820
Is that... mold?

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:29.820
Is that really written there?

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:31.300
Actually, Marie,

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:33.860
don't you think Burgundy's 
climate this year

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:36.260
resembles the climate of the year

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:38.580
your father moved away for work?

00:15:39.110 --> 00:15:40.620
Five years ago?

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:43.170
What does that have to 
do with this writing?

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.590
Dad, come with me!

00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:50.970
I guess Marie thought it was the 
voice of the microbes, too.

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:54.220
How interesting if that were true.

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:57.220
"Everyone Work Together"

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:03.160
It really is cold.

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:06.570
It was like this five years ago, too.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:09.800
There was a lot of rain between 
summer and the harvest.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:13.630
We had a late harvest and 
an early frost that year.

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:16.620
Five years ago...

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:19.100
It was colder inside the 
winery than outside,

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:20.950
so the fermenting took longer.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:24.440
<i>The year I left here.</i>

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:25.580
Back then,

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:28.540
we kept the winery 
from getting too cold

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:30.340
by opening the hallway windows.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:34.470
<i>Marie has looked after 
this domaine in my stead,</i>

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:37.100
<i>and she has absorbed much in that time.</i>

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:40.590
<i>Far more than I have.</i>

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:47.000
Try to avoid anything that 
comes out of his mouth.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:48.300
He is contagious.

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:50.730
If his condition hasn't 
settled by tomorrow,

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:52.700
bring him to my hospital.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:55.110
I have given him something 
to regulate the intestines.

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:58.350
Okay, thank you very much.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.520
An emergency at this hour...

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:10.360
It's just gastro.

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:12.430
Gastro?

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:14.300
It's a French name for a stomachache.

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:18.480
Something like a colloquial 
name for a norovirus infection.

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:21.430
What raw foods are there in Burgundy?

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:22.630
I wonder if he ordered

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:24.560
someone to make sashimi for him again?

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:27.530
Call the front desk and

00:17:27.530 --> 00:17:29.290
have them put you in another room.

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:31.320
We'll really be in a mess 
if you catch this, too.

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:33.320
It's fine. I'll stay here.

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.600
Tell me if you need to throw up.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.330
Where did you get raw oysters, anyway?

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:43.060
I just really wanted some...

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:46.330
So I sent someone to Paris to buy them.

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.640
And look what it's done to me.

00:17:49.990 --> 00:17:53.990
Ow... that doctor should have 
left an anti-diarrheal...

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:56.470
It's not good to be selfish like that.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:59.770
Besides, norovirus multiplies within 
the stomach, so you can't take

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:01.780
anti-diarrheal drugs, no 
matter how much it hurts.

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:02.970
You have to expel it.

00:18:03.650 --> 00:18:05.660
Otherwise, just stay hydrated.

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:07.410
Apparently, in the western nations,

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:09.640
people drink flat cola 
when they get sick.

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.980
It'll replenish your 
glucose and fluids.

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:15.360
Sounds like the lazy way out.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:19.850
Sorry about before.

00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:22.000
I kind of lost it.

00:18:22.630 --> 00:18:25.620
I came on this trip hoping 
to figure something out.

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:29.120
I was scared.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:35.130
I always felt like I had 
to show you my best side.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:38.990
When we were little, and I 
refused to climb that tree,

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:41.360
you told me to climb it next time.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:43.330
Every time we met from then on,

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:45.770
no matter how old I got to be,

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:48.480
I was afraid you'd pester me again.

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:53.940
I thought, if I could get you to like 
me with something I was good at,

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:58.680
I could sidestep the fact 
that I couldn't climb trees

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:01.060
and you'd be satisfied.

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:05.160
I guess that's still 
how I think, even now.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:10.400
I've just been scrambling 
to make myself look strong.

00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:17.050
I finally came to one conclusion 
through this trip.

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:19.950
Rather, I knew all along,

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:22.800
but I was too scared to say it out loud.

00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:27.240
Just like you, Haruka-san...

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:31.100
I don't think that

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:35.320
marrying you is what I want, either.

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:43.040
Ryuuta-kun... I'm sorry.

00:19:48.090 --> 00:19:52.000
You don't have to climb trees.

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:59.090
The cold is starting to let up.

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:02.090
It's getting warmer!

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:06.600
What is it?

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:09.480
Is there something else 
you want to say to me?

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:13.520
I want you to hear me out.

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Moyashimon

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Episode 10

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe 
Theater

00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe Theater Returns!

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:59.250
L.  casei

00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:58.270
Hi! We're L. casei!

00:21:58.270 --> 00:22:00.110
We vigorously keep the activities of

00:22:00.110 --> 00:22:01.570
bad bacteria in check

00:22:01.570 --> 00:22:04.570
until they're ejected 
from the intestines...

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:06.970
Are you sure you should 
say that so openly?

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:07.890
What? What was that?

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:09.220
E.  coli

00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:10.330
Everything that people in Japan put

00:22:09.470 --> 00:22:19.650
Pharmaceutical 
Affairs Law 

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:19.650
Health Promotion Law 

00:22:10.330 --> 00:22:13.220
into their mouths is 
either food or medicine.

00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:16.000
You yogurt guys aren't medicine,

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:18.860
so you can't tell people they'll 
feel better if they eat you!

00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:20.190
What?!

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:21.280
If you want to say that,

00:22:21.280 --> 00:22:23.060
then get classified as a 
designated health food!

00:22:23.060 --> 00:22:24.150
Designated health food?

00:22:24.150 --> 00:22:26.580
Foods designated for specific health uses

00:22:25.380 --> 00:22:35.540
Approved for Consumption
Foods Designated for Specific Health Uses

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:35.910
Part of the 
System for 
Regulation 
of Health 
Foods

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:29.180
are those with irrefutable data 
backing up their healthful effects.

00:22:29.180 --> 00:22:32.460
Only foods classified as such by the 
national government can claim the title.

00:22:32.460 --> 00:22:35.050
That sounds complicated...

00:22:35.050 --> 00:22:36.960
By the way, there are 
foods classified as

00:22:36.330 --> 00:22:36.460
Conditional

00:22:36.460 --> 00:22:40.210
Conditional

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:38.840
"conditional designated health foods,"

00:22:38.840 --> 00:22:40.940
which are known to have health benefits

00:22:40.210 --> 00:25:00.020
Conditional

00:22:40.940 --> 00:22:43.640
but haven't achieved the strict 
classification of designated health foods.

00:22:43.640 --> 00:22:46.730
However, this must be written 
on the product's packaging.

00:22:43.840 --> 00:25:00.020
The health benefits of this product may not be confirmed.

00:22:46.730 --> 00:22:49.700
How confusing...
